    "title": "Family emergency scams are on the rise, experts inform on precautions - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Rachel Gomez Ramirez ,\n12 hours ago WICHITA FALLS, Texas (KAUZ) - A new scam is on the rise throughout Texoma, where fraudsters imitate a family member in desperate need. Tracey Halley Terrell, President of the Oklahoma Bondsman Association, stresses the importance of staying alert to jail scams. These are when a family member receives a phone call of their loved one in jail and urgently needing money, when in reality, it’s all an elaborate scheme by a scammer to try to steal your money. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
